<h2>What Is a Skill</h2>
<p>A Claude Skill is a <strong>reusable work package built to teach a particular way of working</strong>. The core is not growing an individual's ability but making sure that <strong>whoever uses it inside the organization gets results of the same quality</strong> &mdash; that is, turning a personal knack into <strong>organizational knowledge</strong>.</p>

<h3>Why it matters to an organization</h3>
<ul>
    <li>When one person builds a skill and <strong>distributes it to everyone</strong>, everyone produces results of <strong>consistent quality</strong> with the same skill.</li>
    <li>It is closely tied to agent <strong>governance</strong>, organizational policy, and workflows.</li>
    <li>You <strong>have to be able to build skills yourself</strong>. Internal work is only known internally, so it is hard to take something built outside and use it as is. Only when an <strong>ecosystem</strong> for building and refining them in-house is in place do you use a coding agent freely.</li>
</ul>

<h3>In substance it is just a folder</h3>
<p>Inside a skill there is a folder holding <strong>instructions, scripts, and resources</strong>. In computing terms it is <strong>just files and folders, a single archive</strong>. There is no impressive executable, only scripts and resources &mdash; but the fact that these are <strong>loaded dynamically at the moment they are needed</strong> carries great significance.</p>

<h3>A 'work onboarding document' you hand to Claude</h3>
<p>A skill is like a <strong>work onboarding document</strong> you hand to the Claude you use.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>When</strong> should this work be done</li>
    <li>In <strong>what order</strong> should it be handled</li>
    <li>By <strong>what criteria</strong> is the result judged</li>
    <li>What are our <strong>quality standards</strong></li>
</ul>
<p>Telling it these things so it builds things <strong>to your own taste</strong> is where a skill begins. We are all using general-purpose agents, and turning one into a <strong>specialized agent that fits my work</strong> makes a skill essential.</p>
